    route_and_deliver reads the card, takes the locks and calls the route
    (SSH task 0, Claude Opus 5.5, unreviewed: moved there unchanged, D18).
    The route's Delivery decides the rest: words to stdout on exit 0, else
    to stderr; every warning to stderr; then its exit code.

    SSH S3 (Claude Opus 5.5, unreviewed): `--origin <id>` (D25), which a
    far tc's ssh route puts on the remote command. A far key with no
    forced command runs tc send itself, so send files the id as the gate
    does (deliver_once): an id already filed is `already delivered`,
    exit 0, nothing written. A bad id shape is a usage error, exit 9
    (origin_argument).

