    P3 fix round 1a (Claude Opus 5.5, unreviewed): D35. `messages` holds
    (path, folder_fd) pairs: the file is opened by its name, path.name,
    in the folder open at folder_fd (the pinned inbox, or its read/),
    never by its path; `path` names it in the words only.

    Each file is opened with O_NOFOLLOW and O_NONBLOCK and read only when
    fstat calls it a regular file of at most MESSAGE_READ_MAX_BYTES, so a
    link put in place of a message is never followed and a FIFO never
    blocks. Line ends print as read_text gave them (universal newlines).

    @interacts  opens, fstats and reads each file by its name in its
                folder's descriptor; prints to stdout.
    @deps       read_regular_file; MESSAGE_READ_MAX_BYTES.
    @complexity O(u + b) over u messages and b bytes read, each file at
                most MESSAGE_READ_MAX_BYTES + 1.
    @alloc      each file's text while it prints; the list of the unshown,
                returned.
    """
    unshown = []
